  "kneel": {"headword": "kneel", "pos": "", "zh": "vi. 跪下", "en": "n. supporting yourself on your knees\nv. rest one's weight on one's knees"},
  "knife": {"headword": "knife", "phonetic": "naif", "pos": "", "zh": "n. 小刀, 匕首\nvt. 切割, 伤害, 切, 戳\nvi. 劈开, 穿过", "en": "n. edge tool used as a cutting instrument; has a pointed blade with a sharp edge and a handle\nn. a weapon with a handle and blade with a sharp point\nv. use a knife on"},
  "knit": {"headword": "knit", "phonetic": "nit", "pos": "", "zh": "v. 编织, 结合", "en": "n. a fabric made by knitting\nn. a basic knitting stitch\nn. needlework created by interlacing yarn in a series of connected loops using straight eyeless needles or by machine\nv. make (textiles) by knitting"},
  "knob": {"headword": "knob", "phonetic": "nɒb", "pos": "", "zh": "n. 把手, 瘤, 旋钮, 球形突出物\nvt. 使有球形突出物\nvi. 鼓起", "en": "n. a circular rounded projection or protuberance\nn. a round handle\nn. an ornament in the shape of a ball on the hilt of a sword or dagger"},
  "knock": {"headword": "knock", "phonetic": "nɒk", "pos": "", "zh": "n. 敲, 敲打, 敲门\nv. 敲击, 互撞, 攻击", "en": "n. the sound of knocking (as on a door or in an engine or bearing)\nn. negative criticism\nn. a vigorous blow\nn. a bad experience"},
  "knot": {"headword": "knot", "phonetic": "nɒt", "pos": "", "zh": "n. 结, 群, 难题\nv. 打结, (使)纠缠", "en": "n. a tight cluster of people or things\nn. any of various fastenings formed by looping and tying a rope (or cord) upon itself or to another rope or to another object\nn. a hard cross-grained round piece of wood in a board where a branch emerged\nn. something twisted and tight and swollen"},
  "know": {"headword": "know", "pos": "", "zh": "v. 知道, 了解, 认识, 确信", "en": "n. the fact of being aware of information that is known to few people\nv. be cognizant or aware of a fact or a specific piece of information; possess knowledge or information about\nv. know how to do or perform something\nv. be aware of the truth of something; have a belief or faith in something; regard as true beyond any doubt"},
  "knowledge": {"headword": "knowledge", "phonetic": "'nɒlidʒ", "pos": "", "zh": "n. 知识, 学问, 认识, 知道", "en": "n the psychological result of perception and learning and reasoning"},
  "knuckle": {"headword": "knuckle", "phonetic": "'nʌkl", "pos": "", "zh": "n. 指节, 蹄爪, 膝关节\nv. 以指节打, 以手指射", "en": "n. a joint of a finger when the fist is closed\nv. press or rub with the knuckles\nv. shoot a marble while keeping one's knuckles on the ground"},
  "lab": {"headword": "lab", "phonetic": "læb", "pos": "", "zh": "n. 实验室, 研究室\n[医] 凝乳酶", "en": "n. a workplace for the conduct of scientific research"},
  "label": {"headword": "label", "phonetic": "'leibl", "pos": "", "zh": "n. 标签, 称号, 商标, 标志\nvt. 贴标签于, 标注\n[计] 标志; 标注; DOS外部命令:用于建立改变或删除磁盘卷标号", "en": "n. a brief description given for purposes of identification\nn. trade name of a company that produces musical recordings\nn. a radioactive isotope that is used in a compound in order to trace the mechanism of a chemical reaction\nn. an identifying or descriptive marker that is attached to an object"},
  "labor": {"headword": "labor", "pos": "", "zh": "n. 劳动, 努力, 工作, 劳工, 分娩\nvi. 劳动, 努力, 苦干\nvt. 详细分析, 使厌烦", "en": "n. a social class comprising those who do manual labor or work for wages\nn. productive work (especially physical work done for wages)\nv. work hard"},
  "labour": {"headword": "labour", "pos": "", "zh": "n. 劳动, 努力, 工作, 劳工, 分娩\nvi. 劳动, 努力, 苦干\nvt. 详细分析, 使厌烦", "en": "n a social class comprising those who do manual labor or work for wages\nn concluding state of pregnancy; from the onset of contractions to the birth of a child\nn a political party formed in Great Britain in 1900; characterized by the promotion of labor's interests and formerly the socialization of key industries\nn productive work (especially physical work done for wages)\nv work hard\nv strive and make an effort to reach a goal\nv undergo the efforts of childbirth"},
  "lace": {"headword": "lace", "phonetic": "leis", "pos": "", "zh": "n. 饰带, 花边, 缎带, 鞋带\nvt. 结带子, 饰以花边\nvi. 系带子\n[计] 全穿孔", "en": "n. a cord that is drawn through eyelets or around hooks in order to draw together two edges (as of a shoe or garment)\nn. a delicate decorative fabric woven in an open web of symmetrical patterns\nv. do lacework\nv. draw through eyes or holes"},
  "lack": {"headword": "lack", "phonetic": "læk", "pos": "", "zh": "n. 缺乏, 无, 不足\nvt. 缺乏, 短少, 不足, 需要\nvi. 缺乏", "en": "n. the state of needing something that is absent or unavailable"},
  "lad": {"headword": "lad", "phonetic": "læd", "pos": "", "zh": "n. 青年, 家伙, 少年, 情人", "en": "n a boy or man\nn a male child (a familiar term of address to a boy)"},
  "ladder": {"headword": "ladder", "pos": "", "zh": "n. 梯, 梯状物, 发迹的途径\nvi. 袜子抽丝, 成名", "en": "n. steps consisting of two parallel members connected by rungs; for climbing up or down\nn. ascending stages by which somebody or something can progress\nv. come unraveled or undone as if by snagging"},
  "lady": {"headword": "lady", "phonetic": "'leidi", "pos": "", "zh": "n. 淑女, 夫人, 女士, 贵妇", "en": "n. a polite name for any woman\nn. a woman of the peerage in Britain"},
  "lag": {"headword": "lag", "phonetic": "læg", "pos": "", "zh": "n. 落后, 囚犯, 迟延, 桶板, 防护套\na. 最后的\nvi. 落后, 蹒跚, 缓缓而行, 滞后\nvt. 落后于, 押往监狱, 加上外套\n[计] 延迟; 落后", "en": "v. hang (back) or fall (behind) in movement, progress, development, etc.\nv. throw or pitch at a mark, as with coins\nv. cover with lagging to prevent heat loss"},
