  "most": {"headword": "most", "pos": "", "zh": "n. 最多, 最大\na. 大多数的, 几乎全部的, 最多的\nadv. 最, 最多, 极其", "en": "a. (superlative of `many' used with count nouns and often preceded by `the') quantifier meaning the greatest in number\na. the superlative of `much' that can be used with mass nouns and is usually preceded by `the'; a quantifier meaning the greatest in amount or extent or degree\nr. used to form the superlative\nr. very"},
  "mostly": {"headword": "mostly", "pos": "", "zh": "adv. 大概, 大部分, 主要\n[经] 大部份", "en": "r in large part; mainly or chiefly\nr usually; as a rule"},
  "motel": {"headword": "motel", "pos": "", "zh": "n. 汽车旅馆", "en": "n. a motor hotel"},
  "mother": {"headword": "mother", "pos": "", "zh": "n. 母亲, 修女院长\nvt. 产生, 照看, 收养", "en": "n. a woman who has given birth to a child (also used as a term of address to your mother)\nn. a stringy slimy substance consisting of yeast cells and bacteria; forms during fermentation and is added to cider or wine to produce vinegar\nn. a term of address for an elderly woman\nn. a term of address for a mother superior"},
